.el .ds Aq '
.TH memnoth 1  "memnoth 0.1.0-beta.2" 
.SH NAME
memnoth \- Terminal agent, bi\-temporal vault, code graph and MCP server
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmemnoth\fR [\fB\-\-root\fR] [\fB\-\-vault\fR] [\fB\-\-namespace\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-trust\-folder\fR] [\fB\-\-resume\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
One binary for the whole local product.
.PP
With no verb it opens the session against the current directory: the transcript, the vault and what the graph knows, in one screen. Every verb answers as text for a person, or as JSON with \-\-json for a program — the same shapes the MCP tools return, so a script and an agent read one representation rather than two that can drift.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Workspace to read. Defaults to the current directory
.TP
\fB\-\-vault\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Vault database. Defaults to `~/.memnoth/vault.db`
.TP
\fB\-\-namespace\fR \fI<NAME>\fR [default: default]
Vault namespace (`default`, or a name that selects `vault\-<name>.db`)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Machine\-readable output: one JSON envelope on stdout
.TP
\fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress progress lines; keep the answer
.TP
\fB\-\-trust\-folder\fR
Trust this folder without asking first
.TP
\fB\-\-resume\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Resume the named session instead of starting a new one
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
memnoth\-session(1)
Open the session (the default when no verb is given)
.TP
memnoth\-ask(1)
Ask one question and print the answer; no TUI
.TP
memnoth\-vault(1)
Create, read, and correct the temporal vault
.TP
memnoth\-kg(1)
Build and query the code graph
.TP
memnoth\-mcp(1)
Serve the graph over MCP, and register clients for it
.TP
memnoth\-auth(1)
Authentication: login, logout, status, whoami
.TP
memnoth\-config(1)
Configuration: get, set, list, edit
.TP
memnoth\-update(1)
Check for and apply updates
.TP
memnoth\-completion(1)
Shell completion: generate or install completions
.TP
memnoth\-doctor(1)
Report what is wired: paths, versions, profiles, clients
.TP
memnoth\-version(1)
Print the version, build target and commit
.TP
memnoth\-skills(1)
Skill management: add, list, remove, run, edit
.SH EXTRA
Run `memnoth doctor` when something is not wired: it reports the vault, the graph, the MCP server binary it can find and the clients whose config it can read.
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0\-beta.2
